# Architecture

- Use this layering unless the repo already uses a different validated pattern:
  - controller
  - service
  - repository
  - domain/model
  - dto
  - mapper
  - config
- Keep DTOs separate from entities.
- Prefer explicit mappers over leaking JPA entities directly to the API layer.
- Use domain-focused service names.
- Avoid god services and utility dumping grounds.
- Keep transactions in service layer boundaries.
- For cross-cutting concerns, prefer Spring mechanisms such as filters, interceptors, advice, configuration, or dedicated components.
